==Finnish==

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|urj-pro|fi}} {{m|urj-pro|*kaðʲa-||to leave}}. Cognates are found in almost every Uralic language, e.g. {{etyl|se|-}} {{m|se|guođđit||to leave something, to depart}}, {{etyl|sms|-}} {{m|sms|kue´đđed||to leave smth}}, {{etyl|mdf|-}} {{m|mdf|кадомс||to leave}}, {{etyl|chm|-}} {{m|chm|кодаш||to stay}}, {{etyl|udm|-}} {{m|udm|кыльыны||to stay}}, {{etyl|hu|-}} {{m|hu|hagy||to let, to leave}}, {{etyl|mns|-}} {{m|mns|хули||to leave}}, {{etyl|sel|-}} {{m|sel|||to leave|tr=/quəčə-/}}. Labialization of the stem vowel occurred in Proto-Finnic, compare {{etyl|et|-}} {{m|et|kadu||loss}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{hyphenation|ka|to|lang=eo}}
* {{rhymes|ɑto|lang=fi}}
* {{IPA|lang=fi|[ˈkɑto]}}

====Noun====
{{fi-noun}}

# [[failure|Failure]] of [[crop]]s.
# [[loss|Loss]], [[disappearance]], [[lack]]; used primarily in compound terms.
#: ''[[yleisö]]'''kato''''' = lack or loss of audience

